   "source": [
    "# RMSDE vs LDM: Intuition-First Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is a compact teaching companion for your `run/ldm.py` pipeline and the Riemannian Score-SDE code in `libraries/riemannian-score-sde`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Goals:\n",
    "1. Build conceptual intuition for what changes from Euclidean score diffusion to Riemannian score diffusion.\n",
    "2. Strip both codebases to the mathematical core (forward SDE, reverse SDE, sampler).\n",
    "3. Run side-by-side toy simulations.\n",
    "4. Show a setting where Euclidean ambient diffusion is geometrically wrong and a Riemannian formulation is correct.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1) Conceptual comparison (LDM-style Euclidean vs RMSDE)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Euclidean (your `run/ldm.py`)\n",
    "- Data lives in a vector space $\\mathbb{R}^d$ (your VAE latent tensor flattened conceptually).\n",
    "- Forward process is VP diffusion (OU-like):\n",
    "  $$d\\mathbf{x}_t = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\beta(t)\\mathbf{x}_t dt + \\sqrt{\\beta(t)}d\\mathbf{W}_t$$\n",
    "  with marginal form used in training:\n",
    "  $$\\mathbf{x}_t = \\alpha(t)\\mathbf{x}_0 + \\sigma(t)\\boldsymbol{\\epsilon}, \\quad \\epsilon\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I).$$\n",
    "- Model learns $\\epsilon_\\theta(\\mathbf{x}_t,t)$ by MSE against true $\\epsilon$.\n",
    "- Sampling uses discrete reverse updates (DDPM ancestral in `diffusion/sampling.py`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Riemannian (RMSDE)\n",
    "- Data lives on a manifold $\\mathcal{M}$ with metric $g$ (e.g. sphere, SO(3), hyperbolic space).\n",
    "- Forward noising is manifold diffusion (e.g. Brownian on $\\mathcal{M}$).\n",
    "- Score is intrinsic: $\\nabla_{\\mathcal{M}}\\log p_t(x)\\in T_x\\mathcal{M}$ (tangent space), not ambient Euclidean gradient.\n",
    "- Reverse updates are tangent updates followed by retraction/exponential map back to the manifold.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why geometry matters\n",
    "Riemannian geometry matters when:\n",
    "- data is constrained (unit-norm embeddings, rotations, SPD matrices, hyperbolic embeddings),\n",
    "- Euclidean interpolation/noise exits the valid set,\n",
    "- intrinsic distances/topology differ from ambient Euclidean distances.\n",
    "\n",
    "In those cases, Euclidean score models can allocate probability off-manifold and learn wrong denoising directions. RMSDE enforces geometry in both noising and denoising."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Codebase deconstruction to mathematical cores\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 Euclidean core in your `run/ldm.py` stack\n",
    "\n",
    "From `run/ldm.py` and `diffusion/vp_equation.py`:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Training perturbation:\n",
    "  $$x_t = \\alpha(t) z + \\sigma(t)\\epsilon$$\n",
    "  implemented as `x_t = alpha_b * z + sigma_b * noise`.\n",
    "- Network predicts noise `eps_hat = model(x_t, t)`.\n",
    "- Loss:\n",
    "  $$\\mathcal{L}=\\mathbb{E}\\|\\epsilon_\\theta(x_t,t)-\\epsilon\\|^2.$$\n",
    "- Sampling (`DDPM_ancestral_sampler`) uses $\\hat x_0$ estimate then ancestral transition to $t-\\Delta t$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Variable mapping (your code):\n",
    "- $z$ -> `z`\n",
    "- $\\epsilon$ -> `noise`\n",
    "- $x_t$ -> `x_t`\n",
    "- $\\epsilon_\\theta$ -> `eps_hat`\n",
    "- $\\alpha,\\sigma,\\bar\\alpha$ -> `alpha_fn`, `marginal_prob_std_fn`, `alpha_bar_fn`\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.2 RMSDE core in `libraries/riemannian-score-sde`\n",
    "\n",
    "From `riemannian_score_sde/sde.py`, `riemannian_score_sde/losses.py`, and `riemannian_score_sde/sampling.py`:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Forward manifold Brownian SDE (compact manifold case):\n",
    "  $$dX_t = \\sqrt{\\beta(t)}dB_t^{\\mathcal{M}}.$$\n",
    "- DSM loss matches model score to intrinsic transition score:\n",
    "  $$\\mathcal{L}_{DSM}=\\mathbb{E}_{t,x_0,x_t}\\|s_\\theta(x_t,t)-\\nabla_{\\mathcal{M}}\\log p(x_t|x_0)\\|_{g}^2.$$\n",
    "- Reverse-time SDE (in the library abstraction):\n",
    "  $$dX_t = [f(X_t,t)-g(t)^2\\nabla_{\\mathcal{M}}\\log p_t(X_t)]dt + g(t)d\\bar B_t^{\\mathcal{M}}.$$\n",
    "- Sampler step (`GRW` predictor): sample tangent Gaussian, add drift in tangent space, map back via exponential map.\n",
    "\n",
    "Variable mapping (RMSDE code):\n",
    "- manifold -> `cfg.manifold` / `data_manifold`\n",
    "- forward SDE -> `Brownian` / `Langevin` in `riemannian_score_sde/sde.py`\n",
    "- score model -> `model(y,t,context)` in `run.py`\n",
    "- reverse sampler -> `get_pc_sampler(... predictor=\"GRW\")`\n",
    "- manifold retraction -> `manifold.exp(...)` in predictor update\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(7)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---------------------------\n",
    "# Shared VP schedule (mirrors your ldm.py setup)\n",
    "# ---------------------------\n",
    "BETA_MIN = 0.1\n",
    "BETA_MAX = 20.0\n",
    "\n",
    "def beta_t(t):\n",
    "    return BETA_MIN + (BETA_MAX - BETA_MIN) * t\n",
    "\n",
    "def int_beta(t):\n",
    "    return BETA_MIN * t + 0.5 * (BETA_MAX - BETA_MIN) * t**2\n",
    "\n",
    "def alpha_bar(t):\n",
    "    return np.exp(-int_beta(t))\n",
    "\n",
    "def alpha_t(t):\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(alpha_bar(t))\n",
    "\n",
    "def sigma_t(t):\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(np.clip(1.0 - alpha_bar(t), 1e-12, 1.0))\n",
    "\n",
    "def wrap_angle(theta):\n",
    "    return (theta + np.pi) % (2 * np.pi) - np.pi\n",
    "\n",
    "def theta_to_xy(theta):\n",
    "    return np.stack([np.cos(theta), np.sin(theta)], axis=-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "def xy_to_theta(xy):\n",
    "    return np.arctan2(xy[:, 1], xy[:, 0])\n",
    "\n",
    "def kl_div(p, q, eps=1e-9):\n",
    "    p = p + eps\n",
    "    q = q + eps\n",
    "    p = p / p.sum()\n",
    "    q = q / q.sum()\n",
    "    return float(np.sum(p * np.log(p / q)))"
   ]
  },
